# BenChanTech — environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. This file carries NO real values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Analytics 4 (GA4) + Consent Mode v2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONLY runtime environment variable this site reads.
#
# Read in two places, both of which render nothing when it is unset:
#   components/GoogleAnalytics.tsx  — `if (!measurementId) return null;`
#   components/ConsentBanner.tsx    — the banner does not render without it
#
# Set it in Vercel for Production, Preview and Development. The live Benchantech
# web stream ID is recorded in README.md and docs/legal-analytics.md; it is not a
# secret, but it is not duplicated here so this file stays a template.
#
# Consent defaults (analytics_storage denied, all ad_* denied, wait_for_update
# 500, ads_data_redaction on) are hardcoded in components/GoogleAnalytics.tsx and
# are NOT configurable by environment. See tests/analytics-frozen.test.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WYS_AGGREGATE_ENABLED — the Watch Your Step first-party aggregate endpoint
# (plan §8.6) is a BUILD-TIME CONTENT CONSTANT, not an env var. It ships false
# and the counter is not built (plan Q12). It is a constant so that the Data page
# sentence describing the counter (plan Q22) is absent from the DOM whenever the
# counter is off — a runtime env var could flip the claim without flipping the
# implementation, which is exactly the false-claim-fixed-in-copy failure that
# plan R8 forbids. Change it in code, in the same commit as the implementation.
#
# PORT — not application configuration. `PORT=3999 npm run build` only moves the
# port that scripts/guard-next-build.mjs probes so a running dev server on 3000
# does not block a build. Do not modify or bypass that guard.
